// (already waived by nanosoc-multicore-system/lint/hal.tcl): LCVARN
// ── Style waivers ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Numeric literals in port widths (e.g. [31:0]) are standard practice
// (already waived by nanosoc-multicore-system/lint/hal.tcl): STYVAL
// Line length — 120 chars is acceptable for modern editors
// (already waived by nanosoc-multicore-system/lint/hal.tcl): MAXLEN
// Per-port and per-signal comments are overkill for clear code
// (already waived by nanosoc-multicore-system/lint/hal.tcl): COMIOP
// (already waived by nanosoc-multicore-system/lint/hal.tcl): COMDEC
// (already waived by nanosoc-multicore-system/lint/hal.tcl): COMEND
// Always-block comments — not required for well-structured code
